---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const githubInstallUrl = "https://github.com/apps/striff-app/installations/new";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Pricing | Striff"
  description="Free for public repositories. Private-repo teams pay based on active repos (repos that actually generated a diagram), starting at $29/mo for up to 5."
  canonical="https://striff.io/pricing"
>
  <main class="pricing-page text-slate-900">
    <section class="mx-auto flex max-w-[90rem] flex-col gap-8 px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-600" data-reveal>Pricing</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 md:text-5xl" data-reveal>
          Free for public repos. Private repos cost one of three flat monthly prices.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600" data-reveal>
          Start free on public pull requests. Private repos are billed at <strong>$29, $59, or $149 a month</strong>, flat. Which one you land on follows how many repos were actually <strong>active</strong> (generated a diagram) that period, not how many you connected, so connect as many as you like. Your price never changes in the middle of a billing period, and a fully quiet month drops to $0.
        </p>
        <!-- The tiers are price points you land on, not a choice made up front, and the whole
             point of banding rather than metering is that the bill is predictable. So the two
             questions a band raises (what happens when I cross one, and when does it bite)
             get answered here, above the cards, rather than below them. -->
        <p class="pricing-note" data-reveal>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="15" height="15" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 1.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 1 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 1 0-13ZM8 4a.9.9 0 1 0 0 1.8A.9.9 0 0 0 8 4Zm.75 3.5a.75.75 0 0 0-1.5 0v4a.75.75 0 0 0 1.5 0Z"/></svg>
          <span>Every paid plan is the same product. The only thing that changes is how many repos can be active. Nothing to pick up front either: every tier below starts with the same install. Crossing a band never stops a review and never charges you mid-period. Striff keeps analyzing every repo you have enabled, and next month's bill reflects how active you were this month. Prices are USD, billed through Stripe.</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-4 items-stretch" data-reveal>
        <!-- Free -->
        <article class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-md">
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-400">Free</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">$0</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Public repositories</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Chrome extension</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Automated GitHub App checks on public PRs</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Architecture diagrams on any public PR</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Risky-dependency warnings</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Metrics dashboard</li>
          </ul>
          <!-- The secondary link sits above the button so that the primary CTA is the last
               element in every card and the four buttons land on one line. With the link
               below it, this card's button floated a row higher than the other three. -->
          <div class="mt-auto flex flex-col gap-2">
            <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/striffs-for-github/gcbcjajnjbplgkhnbemlkadgnjnfjoen" class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center py-2 text-xs font-medium text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get the browser extension</a>
            <a href={githubInstallUrl} class="btn-secondary inline-flex w-full justify-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Install free</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Starter -->
        <article class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-md">
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-400">Starter</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">$29<span class="text-base font-medium text-slate-400">/mo</span></h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Up to 5 active repos. Sized for one team.</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Checks on every private PR</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> 12 structural checks plus your documented rules</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Metrics dashboard</li>
          </ul>
          <a href={githubInstallUrl} class="btn-secondary mt-auto inline-flex w-full justify-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Install the GitHub App</a>
        </article>

        <!-- Team (featured) -->
        <article class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border-2 border-blue-500 bg-white p-6 shadow-lg ring-1 ring-blue-500/10">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-blue-600">Team</p>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-blue-50 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">Recommended</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">$59<span class="text-base font-medium text-slate-400">/mo</span></h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Up to 15 active repos. Two or three teams.</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Same product as Starter, 3x the repos</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Email support</li>
          </ul>
          <a href={githubInstallUrl} class="btn-primary mt-auto inline-flex w-full justify-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Install the GitHub App</a>
        </article>

        <!-- Scale -->
        <article class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-md">
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-400">Scale</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">$149<span class="text-base font-medium text-slate-400">/mo</span></h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Up to 50 active repos. Several teams.</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Same product as Team, 50 repos</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-500">✓</span> Email support</li>
          </ul>
          <a href={githubInstallUrl} class="btn-secondary mt-auto inline-flex w-full justify-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Install the GitHub App</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <!-- Enterprise bar -->
      <div class="flex flex-col items-start justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 md:flex-row md:items-center" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-400">Enterprise</p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">50+ repos, self-hosted, or compliance needs</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">Private deployment, SSO, audit workflows, and dedicated support.</p>
          <!-- Crossing the Scale cap holds billing at Scale rather than escalating or failing
               (ActiveRepoTierSyncJob leaves the price alone above 50). That is the answer to
               "what happens if we outgrow the top plan", so it belongs on the page. -->
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Go past 50 active repos and you stay at $149 while we get in touch to work out a plan that fits. Nothing changes without a conversation.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary inline-flex shrink-0">Talk to us</a>
      </div>

      <!-- How it works -->
      <div class="mt-6" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">How billing works</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-6 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600 md:grid-cols-3">
          <p><strong class="text-slate-900">1.</strong> Install the GitHub App and connect as many private repositories as you want. Connecting is always free.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-slate-900">2.</strong> Your tier is based on how many of those repos actually <strong>generated a diagram</strong> during your billing period, not how many you've connected. It adjusts automatically in both directions: upgrades and downgrades apply from your <strong>next invoice</strong>, never mid-period, and a fully quiet month drops to $0.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-slate-900">3.</strong> Stripe handles billing: invoices, cancellation, and the customer portal are all self-serve.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
